description: The README still says design decisions land in DECISIONS.md with the next number, while decisions now start as git-issue issues (the corpus proposal went that way). One of the two should go.
 
 If git-issue is the record, the README's maintenance line and its "numbered D10 to D217" pointer should say where a new decision goes and how DECISIONS.md is kept in step. If DECISIONS.md stays the record, the issue is only the proposal. Which do you want?

## Comments
[2026-10-25T05:59:02Z] Matt Parrett: Decided: DECISIONS.md stays the record. An issue is the proposal and the discussion; once settled, the PR that lands it writes the D-entry with the next number, dated, and amends any earlier entry it changes in place (D228 through D231 all went this way). The README's maintenance line is right as it stands; the one addition is a sentence that a decision starts as a board issue and the issue id goes in the D-entry, which the next docs PR can carry.
